{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6109214","formula":"C₂₁H₂₂ClNO","hill":"C21H22ClNO","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":22.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"JWH-203","ru":"JWH-203"},"descriptions":{"en":"JWH-203 (1-pentyl-3-(2-chlorophenylacetyl)indole) is an analgesic chemical from the phenylacetylindole family that acts as a cannabinoid agonist with approximately equal affinity at both the CB1 and CB2 receptors, having a Ki of 8.0 nM at CB1 and 7.0 nM at CB2. It was originally discovered by, and named after, John W. Huffman, but has subsequently been sold without his permission as an ingredient of synthetic cannabis smoking blends.","ru":"JWH-203 (1-пентил-3-(2-хлорфенилацетил)индол) — анальгетик, фенилацетилиндол, действующий как каннабиноидный агонист с практически равным сродством с CB1 и CB2 рецепторами. Так, ингибиторная константа, показывающая степень сродства к CB1, составляет 8 нМ. Был создан химиком Джоном Хаффманом в экспериментальных целях, откуда и сокращение «JWH»."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":44397500,"mass":339.9,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCN1C=C(C2=CC=CC=C21)C(=O)CC3=CC=CC=C3Cl","inchikey":"YDINKDBAZJOSLV-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2-chlorophenyl)-1-(1-pentylindol-3-yl)ethanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"44397500","atoms":46,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.315,"y":1.065,"z":2.416,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.203,"y":-1.359,"z":0.258,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.066,"y":-0.074,"z":-0.707,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.288,"y":0.712,"z":-1.108,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.124,"y":1.206,"z":0.079,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.056,"y":-1.392,"z":-0.308,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.73,"y":-1.727,"z":-0.028,"el":"C"},{"x":0.055,"y":-0.565,"z":-0.272,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.307,"y":2.082,"z":-0.345,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.794,"y":0.434,"z":-0.688,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.059,"y":2.622,"z":0.8